sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Viewer as Player (hls.js)
    participant API as API function
    participant KEYS as S3 keys
    participant CF as CloudFront media
    participant S3 as S3 processed

    Viewer->>API: GET /v1/videos/:id/playback<br/>(session and unlock token optional)<br/>#nbsp;
    API->>API: One access rule: owner, visibility,<br/>password, membership, moderation<br/>#nbsp;
    alt Not allowed
        API-->>Viewer: 404 hidden, 403 removed,<br/>locked or under review<br/>#nbsp;
    else Allowed
        API-->>Viewer: master URL, signed query policy<br/>for videos/{id}/*, playback token (2 h)<br/>#nbsp;
    end

    Viewer->>CF: GET master.m3u8?Policy&Signature&Key-Pair-Id
    CF->>CF: Verify the signature,<br/>cache key ignores the query<br/>#nbsp;
    CF->>S3: On a cache miss: GET through OAC
    S3-->>CF: Playlist
    CF-->>Viewer: Master, then the chosen media playlist

    Viewer->>API: GET /v1/videos/:id/key?v=1<br/>with the playback token<br/>#nbsp;
    API->>API: Check the token and<br/>the access rule again<br/>#nbsp;
    API->>KEYS: Read keys/{id}/v1.json
    KEYS-->>API: Key material
    API-->>Viewer: 16 raw bytes, no-store

    loop Every segment
        Viewer->>CF: GET seg_N.ts?Policy...
        CF-->>Viewer: Encrypted segment
        Viewer->>Viewer: Decrypt AES-128-CBC with the<br/>key and the IV of the playlist<br/>#nbsp;
    end
    Note over Viewer,API: After 30 s of playback the player reports a view.<br/>When the grant expires it asks /playback again.
